#
# A merging source listed beside one of its own inputs. `S` merges `*a` and `*b`, so the string `"1"`
# from `B` collides with the integer `1` held from `A`, and `S` reports at /S/1. `R` merges `*s` and
# then `*b` again: the record carried over from `S` already names `B`'s `"1"` as the merged key, and
# `R`'s own collision with `*b` is the same merged key at the same position, so it is recorded once
# and /R/1 is reported once, not twice. Each notice reads "first at L:1,C:9 and again at L:2,C:9.
# The first value is the one evaluated." Two notices, S before R.
#
rule the_held_value_stands_in_both { S."1" == "a" R."1" == "a" }
